From 793a1060b5d60c4da995d92a75b8a6952a1ce8df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 02:11:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gts4lv-common: Override kernel BPF version

Android 16 mainline modules (netd, Tethering, bpfloader) refuse to run
on kernels older than 5.4. The kernel this targets carries the
ExyHyperBrick 4.9 eBPF backport series, which brings the BPF subsystem
to Linux 5.15.178 feature level, so advertise that version, matching
the Galaxy S9 (exynos9810-common) tree that uses the same series.

DO NOT apply this until kernel/samsung/sdm670 carries that backport
series and passes the BPF selftests and bpf_existence_test; overriding
the version on an un-backported 4.9 kernel makes bpfloader/netd fail
and the device will not boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 product.prop | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/product.prop b/product.prop
index a9871d5..1daa6f8 100644
--- a/product.prop
+++ b/product.prop
@@ -8,3 +8,6 @@ ro.lmk.downgrade_pressure=100
 ro.lmk.kill_heaviest_task=true
 ro.lmk.kill_timeout_ms=100
 ro.lmk.use_minfree_levels=true
+
+# eBPF
+ro.bpf.kver_override=5.15.178
-- 
2.43.0

